{
  "_about": "Brazilian forms that should not appear in pt-PT text (docs/content-plan.md §1.5, §10.2). Read by scripts/check-variety.mjs: warnings, never errors, because a deliberate pt-BR example can be right in context. Applied only to pt-PT items (own or inherited variety) and only to the Portuguese-text fields listed in `fields`; never to ptBR.*, note, en, explain, why or translations. In `pattern`, \\b is a Unicode-aware word boundary (accented letters count as letters); matching is case-insensitive on NFC text. `heuristic: true` marks patterns with known false positives. Every entry carries `hits` (must match) and `clean` (must not match): check-variety fails if a pattern stops doing what its examples say. Later items extend this list.",
